<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">House of Bernadotte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–present</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Bernadotte dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The House of Bernadotte is the royal house of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sweden">Sweden</a>, founded by the French marshal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-xiv-john">Jean-Baptiste Bernadotte</a>, who was elected Swedish crown prince in 1810 and became king as Charles XIV John in 1818. Its kings also ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/norway">Norway</a> in personal union until 1905. The dynasty has reigned in Sweden ever since; its present head is King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-xvi-gustaf">Carl XVI Gustaf</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/house-of-bernadotte.jpg" alt="House of Bernadotte" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: arcjgh · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bernadotte_coa.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
